# PX4 parameters for SITL bring-up runs — removes failsafes that confound a test.
# Format: <vehicle_id> <component_id> <name> <value> <type>  (type 6 = int32, 9 = float)
#
# Apply via QGroundControl (Tools > Load from file). In a headless pxh console
# this text format is NOT readable — `param load`/`param import` want BSON. Use
# `droneflight px4-params --file <this file>` and paste the `param set` lines.
#
# ⚠️ SIM_* parameters are SIMULATION-ONLY. Never carry this file to an aircraft.

# --- Data-link loss ---------------------------------------------------------
# 0 = disabled. Required here because `droneflight fly` disconnects when the
# mission completes, which PX4 reads as "GCS lost" and answers with RTL.
#
# This is ALSO a real design decision, not just sim hygiene: this aircraft flies
# autonomously and covertly, and may have no GCS link at all. Left at RTL, it
# would abandon the mission and climb/beeline home the moment a link drops —
# while paying out fiber. See the failsafe-policy note in NAV-FIDELITY.md /
# CLAUDE.md before choosing the flight value.
1	1	NAV_DLL_ACT	0	6

# --- Simulated battery (SITL only) ------------------------------------------
# 0 = disable simulated drain, so a long mission doesn't trip a battery warning
# mid-test. By default SITL drains to SIM_BAT_MIN_PCT (50%) and warns.
1	1	SIM_BAT_DRAIN	0.0	9
